Task 7.7 — Prefix-Only Role Control Experiment

Continue from the completed Task 7.6 implementation.

Objective

Run one narrowly controlled, label-free experiment to determine whether a short role prefix alone changes the local cross-encoder's behavior.

Task 7.6 changed several parts of the reranker input simultaneously:

added role wording
converted the original query into a sentence
added a generic question
replaced some original query boilerplate

Task 7.7 must isolate only the role-prefix effect.

The experiment must use the same frozen depth-50 candidate pools from Task 7.5/7.6.

Do NOT redesign retrieval.

1. Frozen baseline

Use exactly the existing Task 7.5/7.6 frozen depth-50 pools:

validate:1
validate:2
validate:3

