3. Exactly one experimental change

Keep the original reranker query verbatim.

Only prepend a short role marker.

Current-finding format

Original query:

sweating; shortness of breath; palpitations; numbness and tingling

Experimental query:

Current findings: sweating; shortness of breath; palpitations; numbness and tingling

The text after Current findings: must be byte-for-byte identical to the original query.

Do NOT:

rewrite concepts
reorder concepts
add synonyms
remove concepts
convert semicolons to commas
add a question
add explanatory prose
add patient interpretation
add diagnosis names
add demographic information unless it was already part of the original query
change capitalization of the original query
change punctuation inside the original query
Historical/background format

Original example:

child asthma symptoms and clinical information

Experimental:

Historical/background: child asthma symptoms and clinical information

Again, the entire original query must remain exactly unchanged after the prefix.

Use only these two fixed prefixes:

Current findings:
Historical/background:

Do not create additional prefixes.

Do not tune the prefixes.

Do not test alternative wording.

Do not test multiple punctuation variants.

Do not add a trailing question.

This is specifically a prefix-only control experiment.

