19. Interpretation

At the end, classify the result using evidence from the experiment.

Possible outcomes:

Outcome A — Prefix helps

If previously useful/current candidates move from:

nonpositive → positive

without changing candidate pools or evidence contracts, report that the prefix itself appears to affect eligibility.

Do NOT promote it automatically.

Outcome B — Prefix changes scores but does not recover eligibility

If scores move but no previously useful current candidate becomes eligible, conclude that the prefix alone does not solve the demonstrated bottleneck.

Do not tune the threshold.

Outcome C — Prefix harms previously recovered evidence

If previously selected useful evidence becomes ineligible or substantially degraded, report that clearly.

Do not compensate with another arbitrary prefix.

Outcome D — Essentially no meaningful score change

If the prefix has negligible effect, record that the role marker itself has little influence under this model/input configuration.

